  "question": {
    "text": "If the straight line drawn through the point <math> <mrow> <mtext>P</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>3</mn> </msqrt> <mtext>,&nbsp;</mtext> <mn>2</mn></mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;and inclined at an angle <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mi>π</mi> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> with the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> - axis meets the line <math> <mrow><msqrt> <mn>3</mn> </msqrt> <mtext>x</mtext><mo>-</mo> <mn>4</mn> <mtext>y</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mn>8</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </math> at <math> <mrow> <mtext>Q,</mtext></mrow>&nbsp;</math>&nbsp;then the length of <math> <mrow> <mtext>PQ</mtext></mrow> </math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/KT0000470_AnsExp_1_.jpg\" style=\"width: 265px; height: 217px;\" /><br />&nbsp;</p><p>Point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math>&nbsp;can be obtained by using parametric form of a straight line,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mtext>r</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mtext>r</mtext><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> is on <math> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>3</mn> </msqrt> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mn>4</mn> <mtext>y</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> </math>&nbsp; so it will satisfy this equation, hence,&nbsp;<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mtext>r</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>4&#160;</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mtext>r</mtext><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mo>-</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mtext>r</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mn>8</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>r</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mn>8</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#8658;r</mtext><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the length of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PQ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br />&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
